WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.436
-Our next guest is a
Grammy-winning, Tony-nominated

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:05.305
actress you know from shows
like "Modern Love,"

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:07.406
as well as the films
"The Wolf of Wall Street"

00:00:07.406 --> 00:00:08.808
and "Palm Springs."

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:11.578
She stars in "The Resort," which
is streaming now on Peacock,

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:13.246
with new episodes
premiering Thursdays.

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:14.414
Let's take a look.

00:00:14.414 --> 00:00:16.883 line:0%
-[ Breathes deeply ]
Estoy caliente.

00:00:23.856 --> 00:00:25.625
What the [bleep]
does this guy want?

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:28.561
-Oh, yeah, yeah, you can just...

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:31.731
-Oh [bleep]

00:00:33.399 --> 00:00:35.334
Oh, my God.
[ Ringing ]

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:36.469
Pick up your phone.

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:37.703
Pick up your phone,
pick up your phone.

00:00:37.703 --> 00:00:39.739
[ Cellphone vibrates ]

00:00:41.006 --> 00:00:43.076
-Hey. Emma, hey. Where are you?

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:44.444
-Don't look for me.
Don't look for me.

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:45.845
[Bleep]

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:49.182
-Please welcome back to the show
our friend Cristin Milioti.

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:51.951
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:01:00.893 --> 00:01:03.462
Welcome back, Cristin.
I'm so happy you're here.

00:01:03.462 --> 00:01:05.731
-I'm so happy to be back.
Thanks for having me.

00:01:05.731 --> 00:01:08.000
-In the beginning of that clip,
you said, in Spanish --

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.169
You were trying to say,
"I'm hot."

00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:10.470
-That I'm hot.
-But you said, "I'm horny."

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:11.737
-Yeah, they cut off
the first part,

00:01:11.737 --> 00:01:13.105
where I'm clearly
in a wool blanket

00:01:13.105 --> 00:01:14.407
in, like, a tropical location,

00:01:14.407 --> 00:01:16.342
and then I say, "I'm horny,"
instead, by accident.

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:19.445
-Is that indicative of your own
Spanish-speaking skills?

00:01:19.445 --> 00:01:20.880
-It's -- It is.
-Yeah.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:24.784
-Yeah. We -- That was, like --
We had been all hanging out

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:26.119
at the beach during the weekend,

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:29.054
and my co-star,
Luis Gerardo Méndez,

00:01:29.054 --> 00:01:31.223
who is brilliant on the show --
he had been teaching

00:01:31.223 --> 00:01:34.760
me and my other cast member
Nina Bloomgarden

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:36.662
phrases not to say.

00:01:36.662 --> 00:01:38.598
And one of them
was "estoy caliente,"

00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:40.366
which just means, "I'm horny."

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:42.735
But you'd think it would
mean that I'm hot.

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:44.804
And so I did it
to make everyone laugh.

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:46.038
Like, make the crew laugh.

00:01:46.038 --> 00:01:48.174
We were shooting in like
a 200-degree fruit market.

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:52.177
But they kept it,
which is, like, a delight.

00:01:52.177 --> 00:01:53.412
But, also, it made sense,

00:01:53.412 --> 00:01:55.915
because I think that she
also wouldn't know Spanish

00:01:55.915 --> 00:02:00.453
and she would also
be like, "Oh, I'm horny."

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:02.288
-This is a fantastic show
with you

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:03.623
and William Jackson Harper.

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:04.757
He's a wonderful actor.
-Oh! Who I love.

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:07.493
-And you're on a
10-year wedding anniversary

00:02:07.493 --> 00:02:10.028
and you go to a resort, and then
you start investigating

00:02:10.028 --> 00:02:11.965
a decades-old murder.

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:14.066
-That's right.
-This is, like, a very fun idea.

00:02:14.066 --> 00:02:17.270
-Yeah, well, you'd think,
but hijinks ensue.

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:19.605
And that's the thing
that they don't see coming.

00:02:19.605 --> 00:02:22.275
-Yeah, they always --
Almost everything you're in,

00:02:22.275 --> 00:02:23.977
hijinks do, in fact, ensue.

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:25.678
-Oh, I don't -- I get --
Yeah, I don't go anywhere

00:02:25.678 --> 00:02:27.613
where there's
not hijinks, apparently.

00:02:27.613 --> 00:02:30.783
It's like, not by choice, but --
-Yeah. They follow you.

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:33.085
-They follow me. That's true.
Yeah.

00:02:33.085 --> 00:02:35.254
-They pursue.
The hijinks pursue.

00:02:35.254 --> 00:02:37.156
-That's right. Hijinks pursue.

00:02:37.156 --> 00:02:40.226
-You filmed in Puerto Rico.
-Yes.

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:41.794
-Which must have been
incredibly beautiful.

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:43.562
How did you find it?
-Wonderful.

00:02:43.562 --> 00:02:45.431
How did I find it?
I took a plane there.

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:46.765
-Yeah.
-And then --

00:02:46.765 --> 00:02:48.902
-And that's something, like,
the airlines do, right?

00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:50.336
-And they took --
Much to my surprise --

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:51.704
-You buy the ticket,
but they, like, find it.

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:53.972
-Yeah. And I was like,
"Do you guys --" Exactly."

00:02:53.972 --> 00:02:56.543
Yeah, I was like, "You guys know
how to find this or --"

00:02:56.543 --> 00:03:00.480
And they were like, "Ma'am,
get out of the pilot's cabin."

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.715
Yeah. And I was like,
"Can I also have a drink?"

00:03:02.715 --> 00:03:05.217
No. I don't know.
That's, like, a stupid old joke.

00:03:05.217 --> 00:03:07.020
Pilots don't drink.

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:12.024
-Oh, my God.
-Smash. Good night.

00:03:12.024 --> 00:03:15.861
Yeah, no, they found it for me,
and then I got there.

00:03:15.861 --> 00:03:18.364
And I really liked it.

00:03:18.364 --> 00:03:20.599
It's a brutal place to shoot.
-Yes.

00:03:20.599 --> 00:03:22.935
-I mean, I feel silly
ever being like,

00:03:22.935 --> 00:03:26.505
"Oh, the shooting was so --
It was hard."

00:03:26.505 --> 00:03:28.040
Like, it's an incredible job,

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:30.476
but, yeah, every day is
like 100 degrees.

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:33.145
-Shooting in nice,
air-conditioned places is hard.

00:03:33.145 --> 00:03:35.882
-It's great. Totally.
-No, like, they're long days.

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:38.584
-They're long days. And -- Yeah.

00:03:38.584 --> 00:03:41.587
But we were, like, in the
jungle, 100 degree every day,

00:03:41.587 --> 00:03:43.222
our incredible crew
pushing, like,

00:03:43.222 --> 00:03:45.257
giant cranes up mudslides.

00:03:45.257 --> 00:03:46.492
We would have to hold for rain

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:48.795
because it was
a literal rainforest.

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:51.063
And giants bugs --
-So that's on you.

00:03:51.063 --> 00:03:52.731
-So that's actually on us.
And you're right about that.

00:03:52.731 --> 00:03:54.734
-When you go to a rainforest,
you're like, "Ugh, rain."

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:57.503
-Yeah, and I was like, "Rain?"
Yeah, exactly.

00:03:57.503 --> 00:03:59.839
Yeah. This is false advertising.

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:01.207
-Did you come
right out of quarantine

00:04:01.207 --> 00:04:02.341
and go into shooting the show?

00:04:02.341 --> 00:04:03.375
-Oh, yes.
-Yeah.

00:04:03.375 --> 00:04:07.145
-So, when I landed in
Puerto Rico,

00:04:07.145 --> 00:04:10.750
I was tested for COVID and then
went to go visit the set

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:13.586
and kept my mask on
because I was feeling, like,

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:15.787
a little weird, even though
we were shooting outside

00:04:15.787 --> 00:04:18.124
and I thought it was because I
had just been on a plane.

00:04:18.124 --> 00:04:19.592
And, like, sure enough,
20 minutes later,

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:20.927
they were like,
"Oh, you have COVID.

00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:22.028
Right this way."

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:24.663
And they put me in
a hotel room for 12 days

00:04:24.663 --> 00:04:26.733
that I wasn't allowed to leave.

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:29.535
And it was very dark, and I
faced off with my shadow self.

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:33.539
And then we were back. Yeah.

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:35.173
Yeah, I mean, it's incredibly --

00:04:35.173 --> 00:04:37.243
-I mean, that's another thing
where you think like,

00:04:37.243 --> 00:04:39.779
"Oh, if you're going to be in
a hotel for 12 days,

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:41.214
it's got to be Puerto Rico."

00:04:41.214 --> 00:04:43.415
But I bet even the beautiful
views make no difference after

00:04:43.415 --> 00:04:44.716
like the first six hours.

00:04:44.716 --> 00:04:46.719
-Well, because -- Yes.

00:04:46.719 --> 00:04:48.654
Also because the hotel
I was in --

00:04:48.654 --> 00:04:49.988
We all lived in apartments.

00:04:49.988 --> 00:04:51.356
But, you know,
for the first couple days,

00:04:51.356 --> 00:04:54.126
I landed at this hotel
that was above a casino

00:04:54.126 --> 00:04:56.529
and is, like,
known for bachelorette parties.

00:04:56.529 --> 00:04:58.864
So, I was, like, upstairs like

00:04:58.864 --> 00:05:01.033
the little kid in
"The Secret Garden."

00:05:01.033 --> 00:05:03.903
And, like, they --
There were, like, you know,

00:05:03.903 --> 00:05:07.406
drunk bachelorettes on the beach
being like, "Whoo, Kimberly!",

00:05:07.406 --> 00:05:09.875
and then, like, a deejay on
the beach just playing,

00:05:09.875 --> 00:05:11.978
like, the same song by
The Weeknd.

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:16.148
If I hear "Blinding Lights"
by The Weeknd one more time...

00:05:16.148 --> 00:05:19.551
Like, I already started to turn
into, like, a Gotham villain

00:05:19.551 --> 00:05:23.022
in that room, where I just was
like -- Like, you just --

00:05:23.022 --> 00:05:26.025
You're -- It's 12 days
not leaving a single room.

00:05:26.025 --> 00:05:27.226
I would, like, look outside.

00:05:27.226 --> 00:05:29.728
I would peek out the window,
like, all drawn,

00:05:29.728 --> 00:05:33.299
in, like, a white,
sweaty bathrobe from the hotel.

00:05:33.299 --> 00:05:34.666
-I like to think that there
were bachelorette parties

00:05:34.666 --> 00:05:37.603
going to the front desk
and complaining about this woman

00:05:37.603 --> 00:05:38.971
who was, like, peeking out.

00:05:38.971 --> 00:05:43.141
"We're trying to have fun,
and there's a dead woman."

00:05:43.141 --> 00:05:44.843
-Yeah, exactly. Yeah.

00:05:44.843 --> 00:05:46.679
-"There's a ghost of
a dead woman."

00:05:46.679 --> 00:05:49.615
-"This place -- We weren't told
this place was haunted

00:05:49.615 --> 00:05:52.351
when we booked it on
Groupon or whatever."

00:05:52.351 --> 00:05:55.054
Like -- Yeah, I, basically,
just would, like,

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:57.390
glide into view and glare at
them while, like,

00:05:57.390 --> 00:06:00.592
shaking violently
and coughing into my arm.

00:06:00.592 --> 00:06:02.895
And the TV was broken.
I could only watch this one --

00:06:02.895 --> 00:06:05.798
Then the TV was broken, Seth.
Oh, my God.

00:06:05.798 --> 00:06:07.333
-We all had
really hard quarantines.

00:06:07.333 --> 00:06:10.102
-It was crazy. Yeah.

00:06:10.102 --> 00:06:11.403
Oh, that sounds terrible.

00:06:11.403 --> 00:06:13.406
But the TV was
broken, so I could only watch

00:06:13.406 --> 00:06:15.808
"A League of Their Own"
over and over and over again.

00:06:15.808 --> 00:06:18.277
And so, I was -- Which I love
"A League of Their Own."

00:06:18.277 --> 00:06:20.412
But I was just crying
all the time, like,

00:06:20.412 --> 00:06:22.514
in a bathrobe, sweating.

00:06:22.514 --> 00:06:23.716
-This is great.

00:06:23.716 --> 00:06:26.285
I mean, so your nightmare right
now would be

00:06:26.285 --> 00:06:29.756
The Weeknd opening for
"A League of Their Own."

00:06:29.756 --> 00:06:31.723
-Exactly. I would be, like --
[ Gasps ]

00:06:31.723 --> 00:06:34.393
Like, just -- Yeah.
I would start shivering.

00:06:34.393 --> 00:06:37.629
-We've talked about your
desert work in films such as

00:06:37.629 --> 00:06:39.598
"Palm Springs," and now you're
doing some jungle work in this.

00:06:39.598 --> 00:06:40.732
-That's right.

00:06:40.732 --> 00:06:42.267
-Do you have a preference
of where to shoot?

00:06:42.267 --> 00:06:43.703
Because they both seem,
like, pretty...

00:06:43.703 --> 00:06:45.538
-Intense?
-...trying, yeah.

00:06:45.538 --> 00:06:48.073
-Yeah. The jungle.
I like the jungle.

00:06:48.073 --> 00:06:49.675
-Oh, okay. That's nice to hear.
-I like it.

00:06:49.675 --> 00:06:52.311
I love a tree.

00:06:52.311 --> 00:06:54.246
No, but I do. I love...
[ Laughter ]

00:06:54.246 --> 00:06:58.851
It's beautiful.
There's so many great smells.

00:06:58.851 --> 00:07:01.920
There's -- Yeah.
-What a sales pitch.

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:03.055
Do you -- Does the --

00:07:03.055 --> 00:07:05.024
-Yeah. You guys are going to
love the jungle.

00:07:05.024 --> 00:07:09.228
If you like smells
and rain and bugs and mud,

00:07:09.228 --> 00:07:11.564
you are going to love
the jungle.

00:07:11.564 --> 00:07:13.332
But I actually --
I really do like the jungle.

00:07:13.332 --> 00:07:15.968
The desert I don't trust.
-Yeah.

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:17.336
-Why are we out there?
We don't belong there.

00:07:17.336 --> 00:07:18.538
That's like when
we're in a plane.

00:07:18.538 --> 00:07:19.671
Why are we up there?
We don't belong there.

00:07:19.671 --> 00:07:21.273
We're not birds, Seth.

00:07:21.273 --> 00:07:22.875
I don't have to tell you.
-You don't have to tell me.

00:07:22.875 --> 00:07:24.710
I've been saying that
from the beginning.

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:26.712
I was the first guy
who noticed, remember?

00:07:26.712 --> 00:07:29.314
-I forgot. That's right.
You were like, "Wait a second.

00:07:29.314 --> 00:07:31.217
Wait. No."

00:07:31.217 --> 00:07:34.220
Yeah. No, but, yeah,
the desert feels like that,

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:35.321
when, like, there's no water.

00:07:35.321 --> 00:07:36.522
It's hot.

00:07:36.522 --> 00:07:38.357
We're not --
Even lizards have trouble here.

00:07:38.357 --> 00:07:39.792
-Yeah.
-Why are we here?

00:07:39.792 --> 00:07:42.861
-Right. Anybody who's thriving
in the desert looks super-weird.

00:07:42.861 --> 00:07:45.331
-Looks weird.
Spiders underground.

00:07:45.331 --> 00:07:48.701
-Yeah.
-Spiky shrubs.

00:07:48.701 --> 00:07:50.402
-Spiky shrubs.
-Spiky shrubs.

00:07:50.402 --> 00:07:52.938
-No, thank you, spiky shrub.
-No, thanks. Yeah.

00:07:52.938 --> 00:07:54.339
-I'm barely okay
with normal shrubs.

00:07:54.339 --> 00:07:55.641
-That's right, yeah.

00:07:55.641 --> 00:07:57.810
If I've said it once,
I've said it a thousand times --

00:07:57.810 --> 00:07:59.845
I don't mess with
spiky shrubs anymore.

00:07:59.845 --> 00:08:02.214
-Yeah. And, obviously, you don't
want to be messed with

00:08:02.214 --> 00:08:04.316
or else you wouldn't
have evolved into being spiky.

00:08:04.316 --> 00:08:05.851
-Thank you. So why are we here?

00:08:05.851 --> 00:08:09.021
-Yeah. Well, I think we've made
our case against the desert.

00:08:09.021 --> 00:08:10.589
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:08:10.589 --> 00:08:12.625
I'm proudly coming out as
anti-desert.

00:08:12.625 --> 00:08:15.928
-You definitely are. Probably?
-Yeah. Dusty.

00:08:15.928 --> 00:08:18.196
-Well, that's enough?
-Do you love sand in your eyes?

00:08:18.196 --> 00:08:20.065
-Some people in the desert
watch this show. Enough.

00:08:20.065 --> 00:08:23.268
-Well, I have a --
Yeah, I have...

00:08:23.268 --> 00:08:25.004
I do have questions about
living in the desert,

00:08:25.004 --> 00:08:26.105
but we don't have to
get into it now.

00:08:26.105 --> 00:08:27.472
-Maybe next time?
-Okay.

00:08:27.472 --> 00:08:29.642
-Alright. It's this the
best having you here.

00:08:29.642 --> 00:08:30.676
Thank you so much.
-I love being here.

00:08:30.676 --> 00:08:33.345
-You guys,
that's Cristin Milioti.

00:08:33.345 --> 00:08:35.581
"The Resort"
is streaming now on Peacock,

00:08:35.581 --> 00:08:37.383
with new episodes
premiering Thursdays.

00:08:37.383 --> 00:08:39.051
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

